In `patchJar`, each entry is re-created with `new JarEntry(entryName)`, which discards the original entry's metadata (last-modified time, size, compression hint, etc.). For entries that are simply copied through (the majority), this can affect build reproducibility and JAR integrity. Consider copying the relevant attributes from the source entry, e.g.:
```java
JarEntry newEntry = new JarEntry(entryName);
newEntry.setTime(entry.getTime());
// optionally: newEntry.setSize(entry.getSize());
jos.putNextEntry(newEntry);
```
